{
  "version": 2,
  "note": "Retunes every seeded style that carried an absolute spatial treatment parameter onto the relative form introduced in image-tools ops.proto, so a style tuned once holds its look at every delivery surface. A relative value is a fraction of the delivered image's short edge; the pixel figures quoted in the per-style reasons are what each resolves to on web.hero (1440x720). Styles absent from this file carry no spatial parameter and are unchanged.",
  "retune_reasons": [
    "engraved-colonnade.engraving: 7px hatch on a hero frame is below the period where a cross-hatch reads as line rather than as texture; ~11px lets the tone show through.",
    "op-art-interior.line_screen: Op art lives on a bold screen. 6px read as flat grey at hero scale; ~13px restores the figure-ground beat the style is named for.",
    "solar-bloom-horizon.bloom: Same ~18px lift at hero, now held proportional so the glow does not shrink to a rim on a large surface.",
    "stipple-massif.stipple: Same ~7px cell at hero; stipple carries tone through dot count so the grid must stay tight.",
    "swiss-contour.line_screen: Same ~11px pitch at hero, matching the engraving period so the two styles sit together in one catalog.",
    "ascii-field.ascii_mosaic: ~14px = two glyph advances, so characters blit at 2:1 and stay crisp. The previous single-advance cell rendered glyphs too small to read as characters.",
    "memphis-weave.displacement: Same ~18px throw on a ~26px wavelength at hero. Spacing had no effect at all before this phase \u2014 the implementation ignored it.",
    "vaporwave-drift.aberration: Same ~9px channel separation at hero; fringing must scale with the frame or it vanishes on a large surface.",
    "vaporwave-drift.bloom: Same ~22px lift at hero."
  ],
  "surfaces": [],
